WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.134 --> 00:00:00.967
(audience applauding)

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.550
(Kelly drowned out by audience applause)

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.218
- It's nice to see you again.

00:00:05.218 --> 00:00:06.185
- It's good to see you again.

00:00:06.185 --> 00:00:07.040
What's up?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.060
- Yeah. You know, I'm living
my best life, Dr. Phil.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:09.930
How are you?
- Yeah you are, aren't you?

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:10.829
- Yes.

00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:12.270
- You need to find some other stuff to do.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.490
- (laughing) No.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.040
You know what? That's
actually a part of it though.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.200
I only say yes to things that
like really I'm interested in

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.750
and I wanna do, like, at
this point in my career.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.610
And like working with
Snoop on this new show

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.328
that we're doing, it makes me so happy.

00:00:23.328 --> 00:00:24.161
- I know.

00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:24.994
- So like go to work and love it.

00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:25.827
- Yeah, that's the thing.

00:00:25.827 --> 00:00:27.060
You gotta have passion and don't do it

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.090
if you don't want to do it.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:28.923
- Amen.

00:00:28.923 --> 00:00:30.020
- You get where you can
do that, you got it.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:30.990
- Yeah, I know.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:31.992
I'm feeling blessed.

00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:32.825
(audience applauding)

00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:35.590
Well, you discovered TikTok
since we last saw you.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.840
So how's that going?

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.840
- It's fun because people
are getting their information

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.310
in different places, different ways,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.750
so you gotta meet 'em
where they are, right?

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:43.583
- Yeah. Okay.

00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:46.830
Well, what's the TikTok
challenge you're doing here

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.670
'cause this is good?

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.524
- [Dr. Phil] Yeah.

00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:51.700
- [Kelly] First of all, I just
love you're just hanging out

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.974
in the desert, like a
rock star doing a video.

00:00:53.974 --> 00:00:54.807
(audience laughs)

00:00:54.807 --> 00:00:57.200
- Yeah, you gotta go out way in the desert

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.033
to get me to dance.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.361
- (laughing) Where no one saw you.

00:01:00.361 --> 00:01:02.400
- Yeah. I mean, there wasn't
anybody within 30 miles

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.200
except this guy with a drone.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.535
- I love that.

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:06.560
Is that fun to do?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.393
I think those things are fun.

00:01:07.393 --> 00:01:08.226
- Yeah, it really is.

00:01:08.226 --> 00:01:10.820
We were out actually shooting a spot

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.850
for the launch of the season.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:13.683
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:16.637
- And so my son Jordan
said, "Hey do this".

00:01:16.637 --> 00:01:17.600
And I said, "What?"

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.180
And he said, "Just do it,
I'll tell you later." (laughs)

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.330
- See. Sometimes just listen.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.230
- Yeah. Really.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.360
- See. And this is my favorite part,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.510
this getting down, the left, right.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.990
So wait, you also took
to TikTok to tell people

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.190
how to spot a liar.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.610
So how do you do that?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.760
- That's really interesting
'cause there's a lot

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.510
of myths out there, but I've spent a lot

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.884
of time focusing on deception
detection in my career

00:01:39.884 --> 00:01:42.182
and there are ways to
tell if somebody's lying.

00:01:42.182 --> 00:01:43.070
- Okay.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.145
- So watch it.

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:44.978
- I know.

00:01:44.978 --> 00:01:46.510
Here's the thing, I don't feel like I lie

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.640
but I'm not good at catching them.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.510
- Well, when people
meet for the first time

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:54.220
there's usually 10 lies
within the first hour or two.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.370
- What?

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.910
- Yeah, when two people meet,

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.970
somebody tells a lie 10 times
within the first hour or two.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:00.803
- Why would you do that?

00:02:00.803 --> 00:02:01.740
Then you gotta keep up with it.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.990
- Well, it's just trying
to impress, I guess.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.690
But you can tell if people are lying.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.620
Particularly, if they're
being interrogated,

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.070
90% of their time their
feet will be pointed

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.700
towards the exit.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.670
- What?

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.870
- 90% of the time

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.080
their feet will be
pointed towards the exit.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.350
- I'm gonna totally watch
where my feet are pointed

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.183
from now on.

00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:21.400
- And if they repeat the question,

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.320
it's not because they didn't hear you,

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.840
they're buying time so they
can formulate an answer.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:31.193
And thirdly, when you hear
somebody say, "I swear to God"

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.433
the next thing outta
their mouth's a damn lie.

00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:35.266
(Kelly laughing hysterically)

00:02:35.266 --> 00:02:36.099
(audience laughs)

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:38.040
If they invoke the deity,

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.430
the next thing outta their mouth's a lie.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.490
Now you gotta get a baseline
and look at these things

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.400
in clusters.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.350
But those are pretty good rules.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.120
- So wait, what were like the best lies?

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.280
'Cause I have children
and they're five and seven

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.740
so they're at the age where
they do completely lie to me

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.170
to try and get out of
it or blame the other.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.750
What do your kids do sometimes?

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:56.583
- My kids?

00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:57.416
- Yeah.

00:02:57.416 --> 00:02:58.760
- Oh, their lips were moving. Yeah.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.300
- (laughing) And you were like, "Lie"?

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.480
- Their rule is, the first
one to get to mom or dad,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.630
that's who's gonna win.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:06.463
- That's my kids, and race.

00:03:06.463 --> 00:03:09.760
- Yeah, if they knock the lamp
over, first one to get to mom

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.130
or dad's gonna win. "He did it."

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.530
So it's primacy.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.090
Get there, tell your story first,

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.100
you're gonna win every time.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.163
Primacy's key.

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:19.990
- I literally had to talk
to a therapist about this.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.560
'Cause I was like, my
kids, I can't get them...

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.270
and we have like a whole thing you hold

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.282
like you have the time
that you're talking.

00:03:27.282 --> 00:03:28.115
- Yeah.

00:03:28.115 --> 00:03:28.948
- And then the other
person gets to hold it

00:03:28.948 --> 00:03:31.430
'cause it's like they feel
like whoever says it first

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.430
is gonna win the argument.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:33.276
And that's not the case.

00:03:33.276 --> 00:03:34.109
- They're right.

00:03:34.109 --> 00:03:34.942
- No. It's not the case.

00:03:34.942 --> 00:03:35.811
- No. They're right.

00:03:35.811 --> 00:03:36.644
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:36.644 --> 00:03:37.477
(audience laughs)

00:03:37.477 --> 00:03:38.580
- (laughing) It's not the case.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.000
- You go back and score
it up I'll guarantee you,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.810
whoever got to you first, got primacy.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:44.643
- Do you wanna know?

00:03:44.643 --> 00:03:46.434
My kids are not gonna watch this,

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.110
(Dr. Phil chuckles)
(audience laughs)

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.790
but what I do and you can
judge me all you want,

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.290
I will say like, "Well, okay.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.930
I'm gonna have to go look at the cameras."

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.162
There are no cameras (laughs)

00:03:55.162 --> 00:03:57.380
(audience laughs)

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.230
And I swear to God--

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.894
- See.

00:03:59.894 --> 00:04:00.727
(audience laughing)

00:04:00.727 --> 00:04:01.560
- This is real.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.393
(audience applauding)

00:04:02.393 --> 00:04:03.226
I do. I swear to God.

00:04:03.226 --> 00:04:04.110
I'm not lying.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.430
Literally, it will be my son every time

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.987
and go, "No".

00:04:07.987 --> 00:04:09.062
(audience laughs)

00:04:09.062 --> 00:04:10.770
- (laughing) And he will out himself.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.400
As soon as I say, "I'm
gonna watch the cameras"

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.780
Remy B. Is right there.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.170
- See what you're doing
is you just planted

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.960
what's called a mind virus.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.767
You put a mind virus in there that said,

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:20.120
"Oh, I'm gonna go watch the cameras"

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.130
and they go, "Oh my God, wait a minute."

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.230
They try to think, "Was
I in front of the camera?

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.700
Could they see it? I don't know."

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.540
And then they start playing
a game in their head,

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.405
they go, "I did it. I did it. Nevermind."

00:04:29.405 --> 00:04:30.238
- Yeah.

00:04:30.238 --> 00:04:32.130
- But that's called planting a mind virus.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.085
- It's also called finding
out what the damn truth is

00:04:34.085 --> 00:04:34.918
(laughs)

00:04:34.918 --> 00:04:35.751
- Yes. It is.

00:04:35.751 --> 00:04:36.584
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:36.584 --> 00:04:37.417
(audience cheering)

00:04:37.417 --> 00:04:38.500
- 'Cause I'm like, "You're
lying and I know it."

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.112
So congratulations, you and Robin...

00:04:41.112 --> 00:04:43.440
Robin just celebrated,
is it fourth grandchild?

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.273
- Yes, fourth.

00:04:44.273 --> 00:04:45.106
(audience applauding)

00:04:45.106 --> 00:04:46.090
- Gosh. That's cool.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.600
Is it more fun being the grandparent?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.253
- It really is more fun
being the grandparent.

00:04:49.253 --> 00:04:52.540
You know, it's not just a
cliche that you can put 'em down

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.373
and leave.

00:04:53.373 --> 00:04:54.206
- Yeah.

00:04:54.206 --> 00:04:55.039
- That's really cool.

00:04:55.039 --> 00:04:55.872
- Oh, it's (Kelly drowned out by Dr. Phil)

00:04:55.872 --> 00:04:58.280
- And this is a fourth
and it's a little boy.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.560
And so Jordan has a little
girl and a little boy

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.180
and they're just a year apart.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.542
And his name is Grey Oliver.

00:05:04.542 --> 00:05:07.340
- (gasps) What a cool name.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.173
- Yeah.

00:05:08.173 --> 00:05:09.760
- Okay. So you've said family
meetings are important.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.937
I do this with my kids.

00:05:11.937 --> 00:05:14.900
I feel like it's more
helpful for communication.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:15.733
- It really is.

00:05:15.733 --> 00:05:17.870
You know the thing I've
said to people so many times

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:20.180
and they think it's kind
of weird to say it this way

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.730
but you need to talk
your kids about things

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:23.715
that don't matter.

00:05:23.715 --> 00:05:24.750
- Yeah.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.130
- Because that keeps the
line open when it comes time

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.954
to talk about things that do matter.

00:05:30.954 --> 00:05:31.787
(audience applauds)

00:05:31.787 --> 00:05:33.870
If you're talking to
'em about just anything.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:38.177
And if the first time
you ever really sit down

00:05:38.177 --> 00:05:41.860
and talk to your kids is
when it's really important,

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.950
it's gonna feel awkward.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.040
But if you've done it a lot...

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.870
And it's so important, don't sit down

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.800
and talk to 'em like we're talking now,

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.019
they feel conspicuous.

00:05:50.019 --> 00:05:52.590
Talk to 'em while you're
shooting the basketball

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.570
or taking the dog for a walk,

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:55.970
don't put them in the hot seat.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:58.200
Do it when they don't feel so conspicuous.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.599
That's when they start talking to you.

00:06:00.599 --> 00:06:01.432
- Yeah.

00:06:01.432 --> 00:06:03.020
- Don't do like, "Okay,
let me tell you something."

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.404
- I find in the car--

00:06:04.404 --> 00:06:05.800
they're chatty.
- That's great.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.320
Yeah. They can look out the window,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.900
the radio could be playing.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.500
Don't put 'em on the spot,
but talk to 'em about anything

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.740
so when it comes time to
talk to 'em about something

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.136
that really matters,
they don't feel like--

00:06:17.136 --> 00:06:17.969
- You already have that open line

00:06:17.969 --> 00:06:18.802
- What's going on. Yeah.

00:06:18.802 --> 00:06:19.783
- Yeah. That's great advice.

00:06:19.783 --> 00:06:20.694
(audience applauds)

00:06:20.694 --> 00:06:21.535
I love that.

00:06:21.535 --> 00:06:22.859
Well, let's talk about your show.

00:06:22.859 --> 00:06:24.628
So what are you focusing on now?

00:06:24.628 --> 00:06:27.523
- Well, everybody's heard it

00:06:27.523 --> 00:06:30.150
and I've been saying it
for a long, long time,

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:33.703
but this pandemic has really taken a toll

00:06:33.703 --> 00:06:37.600
on mental health with kids, parents alike.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:42.380
But we've seen spikes in
depression and anxiety, loneliness,

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.390
self-esteem worse than we have ever seen

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.490
since records have started being kept.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.830
And everybody thought when
the quarantine was lifted

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:55.120
everybody's gonna go racing
back out like, oh, party time.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.650
A lot of kids have really
regressed and they're intimidated

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.910
by what they used to take for granted.

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:04.127
And they feel like, I don't know,

00:07:04.127 --> 00:07:07.420
"Can I really do that? And
am I gonna be accepted?"

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.880
And I mean, they've just kind
of fallen back developmentally

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.380
and socially and educationally.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.360
And so they're doubting themselves

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.890
and there's just a lot
of issues right now.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.550
And parents can really help

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:23.830
by supporting their
kids, being understanding

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.760
and meeting them where they are right now.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.990
And so we focused on the show a lot

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:31.240
in trying to really bring
families back together again.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:35.608
And I think sitting down,
as corny as it sounds

00:07:35.608 --> 00:07:38.930
and as awkward as it feels
to have a family meeting,

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.820
turn off the TV or put your
phones down, how you feel today?

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.210
'Cause you go to school, we
teach, 'em adding, subtracting,

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:49.630
geography, history, but we
don't teach kids how to feel,

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:52.585
how to manage anxiety, what
if somebody's bullying you?

00:07:52.585 --> 00:07:54.320
That's not part of the curriculum.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.654
So we've gotta make it part of the family.

00:07:56.654 --> 00:07:57.487
- Yeah.

00:07:57.487 --> 00:07:58.320
(audience applauds)

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.746
I love that.

00:07:59.746 --> 00:08:02.110
Well, May is mental
health awareness month.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.720
So what's something helpful

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.380
that you see these days
in terms of mental health?

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.300
Like what's helpful for people?

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:11.170
- Well, I think mostly
is not just awareness

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.340
but taking action.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.857
Ask yourself what can I do in my family

00:08:15.857 --> 00:08:18.520
that's something affirmative
that we haven't been doing

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.490
before?

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:23.339
And if you can find
something with each child...

00:08:23.339 --> 00:08:26.190
If you've got two or
three kids doing something

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.750
with the kids is one thing,

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.900
but finding something special you do

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:34.560
with each child that you don't
do with the other children

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.850
which is just you two, really
makes them feel special.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:39.683
- It does.

00:08:39.683 --> 00:08:40.734
My kids demand dates

00:08:40.734 --> 00:08:42.830
and they don't want the other one around.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.332
- Exactly. They want you.

00:08:44.332 --> 00:08:45.165
- Yeah. We have dates.

00:08:45.165 --> 00:08:46.730
- They want you and
them, just you and them.

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.831
- Yeah.

00:08:47.831 --> 00:08:49.930
- And it doesn't have to be for two hours,

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:51.770
even 15 or 20 minutes.

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:53.820
If you just have that time with them,

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.020
that makes them feel
special, undivided attention,

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.790
it does so much for self-esteem

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.650
you have no idea what it is.

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:01.870
And it can be something silly.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.360
I know with my kids, one of
them used to like to get up

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.920
the top of the stairs
and bomb his army men

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.549
with tennis balls

00:09:08.549 --> 00:09:09.382
(Kelly laughing)

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:10.215
and we'd do it for 15 or 20 minutes

00:09:10.215 --> 00:09:11.630
and set 'em up and bomb them.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:12.540
And they love that.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.300
The other one liked to play with the farm.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.780
and I didn't do either
thing with the other one.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:17.800
And they loved that.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:18.770
It was their special time.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:19.603
They still remember it today.

00:09:19.603 --> 00:09:20.436
(audience applauds)

00:09:20.436 --> 00:09:21.792
- Yeah. I love this.

00:09:21.792 --> 00:09:23.918
So is it true that you still send Oprah

00:09:23.918 --> 00:09:26.730
two thank you letters like a year?

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:27.710
- I do.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:32.190
Oprah and I met in the late
'90s when she was in trial

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.650
and I was on the trial team

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:37.070
and then I started doing the show

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.540
and then started doing the show a lot.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.660
And then we launched the show

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:45.660
and it really changed my life a lot.

00:09:46.372 --> 00:09:48.070
I had a great life when I met her

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:52.000
and I've got a great life
now, but she changed a lot

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.679
of things and it's just
been really important to me

00:09:55.679 --> 00:10:00.679
every year to stop, sit
down and write her a letter

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:05.280
and say, "Thank you for
the impact you've had on me

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.040
and my family."

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.170
And I've done it every
year for 25 or 26 years.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.310
And she told me something one time,

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:15.713
the first time I launched
a book on her show,

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.820
I sent her like huge flower arrangement

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.620
and a thank you note and stuff.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.160
I think she had been on the
air 17 years at that point

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:29.280
and she called me and said,
all the things I've done

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.640
all the books and stuff,

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.600
this is the first time
anybody's ever said thank you.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:34.660
- What?

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.710
- First time anybody's
ever said thank you.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.040
- Oh wow.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.270
- And I thought, wow,

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.434
that's hard to believe.
- That's depressing.

00:10:41.434 --> 00:10:43.089
Yeah.

00:10:43.089 --> 00:10:45.110
- And now I've had my show for 20 years,

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:46.710
I understand what she means.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:47.960
- Oh man.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:48.950
- I understand what she means.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:49.950
And so I don't know.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.370
I've got this value,

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.554
don't forget who brung you to the dance.

00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:58.830
and I've never let her think

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:00.640
I forgot who brung me to the dance.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.193
- Yeah. I love that.

